  "source": "book/assets/specified-region.svg",
  "chapter": "2.1-context-is-the-first-modeling-problem",
  "claim": "*Obligation, scaffolding, and degrees of freedom.* The engineering obligation establishes the minimum consequential content that must be preserved. A particular agent may require additional scaffolding to interpret and satisfy that obligation reliably. Greater agent capability can reduce this scaffolding and leave more implementation choices open, but it does not change the obligation itself.",
